  "hypothesis": "A fixed-origin prepared TextRenderPlan recomputes identical scan-conversion coverage on every draw. Prepare exact uint16coverage once in glyph/row order,retain compact row runs/words and release temporary geometry/events/crossings/row storage. This should remove repeated raster work and substantially reduce retained geometry capacity;extra preparation,temporary overlap and scalar blending costs must be measured rather than presumed.",
  "intendedEndState": "Existing caller-owned plan remains the sole retained owner and admission context. One shared Rasterize loop selects immediate blending or row capture once per row,outside pixel loops. Capture trims zero borders,stores every interior coverage word and retains glyph order. Plan.Draw invokes the unchanged Blend on fresh caller pixels/colors. Temporary TextRasterizer shares the existing root and disposes before publication. No new public API,general cache,pool,independent budget or numerical policy.",
  "proof": "Removing the row-destination branch and restoring nonnullablecanvas reconstructs the entire old Draw loop. Band,geometry/events,coordinates and Blend bodies are verbatim except Blend visibility. Coverage uses the identical uint floor/clamp then lossless ushort storage;zero-border omission performs the same no-op as old zero coverage. Rows are captured in original glyph/row/pixel order,so overlapping glyph composition and per-glyph rounding remain. Plan owner exists before escaping arrays. Grow reserves new+old overlap before allocation,checks cancellation,copies bounded chunks,then releases old charges after actual users. Retained capacity releases only at plan disposal;draw borrows that admission and uses its independent token. Existing geometry/container bounds remain;row data adds only memory/array bounds,not a new quota.",
